	(text "DESIGN NOTE:\nWhen the downstream port is enabled, this pin is set as\nan input with an internal pull-up resistor applied. The\ninternal pull-up enables power to the downstream port\nwhile the pin monitors for an active low overcurrent signal\nassertion from an external current monitor on USB port 1.\nThis pin will change to an output and be driven low when\nthe port is disabled by configuration or by the host control.\np13"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 280.924 221.996 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "3a4c6868-f025-4049-96e4-72c1a7bd7f15")
	)
	(text "DESIGN NOTE:\nWhen bypassing with capacitors of 10 μF and up, it is\ngood practice to place a smaller value capacitor in\nparallel with the larger to handle the high frequency\ncomponents of any line transients. Values in the range\nof 0.01 μF to 0.1 μF are recommended. Again, good\nquality, low-ESR capacitors should be chosen. p. 24"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 77.724 114.046 0)
		(effects
